    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0361" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1530: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-12T22:00:00+09:00">June 12, 1940—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 12—10:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>447. My 429, June 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d391-f1"/> The Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs has sent me as an “informal, oral and unofficial statement” a
                    document marked strictly confidential, the text of which in translation is
                    contained in our immediately following telegram 4[<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >48</hi>], June 12, 11 p.m.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d391-f2"/> He wishes me to
                    understand that it does not commit his Government in any way but that it will
                    serve to indicate certain thoughts which have occurred to him following our
                    conversation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d391-f1" n="65" xml:id="d391-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see memoranda from the Ambassador in Japan, June 10, <ref
